Apache Maven — a tool that does much more than compiling and packaging code. Maven automates dependency management, downloads libraries from repositories, and orchestrates builds through plugins and lifecycles.

three fundamental concepts every Java/Maven developer must know:

Dependencies: Libraries your project needs, declared in pom.xml and auto-managed by Maven.

Repositories: Locations Maven searches for dependencies — local cache, central public repository, and private remote repos.

Build Tools: Software that automates compiling, testing, packaging, and deploying code. Maven’s build lifecycle and plugins power this automation.

